# .gitattributes - line endings are normalized in the repository, not just on one machine.
# Module: build (gitattributes).
# Owns: forcing LF in the index and in every working tree, for all text files.
# Depends: none. Without this, core.autocrlf on Windows hands out CRLF and rule 5 fails.

# The rulebook mandates LF, one final newline, ASCII. git has to agree with that on
# every platform, not only on the machine that happens to have autocrlf off.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Compiled output is never text, and letting git try to normalize it corrupts it.
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.obj binary
*.o binary
*.lib binary
*.a binary
*.pdb binary
*.exe binary
